{number: 131}
{title: O Master, Let Me Walk with Thee}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [C] Master, [F] let me [C] walk with Thee
In [F] lowly [C] paths of [G7] service [C] free;
Tell me Thy [F] secret; [C] help me bear
The [F] strain of [C] toil, the [G7] fret of [C] care.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Help [C] me the [F] slow of [C] heart to move
By [F] some clear, [C] winning [G7] word of [C] love;
They wayward [F] feet in [C] paths to guide
And [F] stay them [C] walking [G7] by Thy [C] side.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Teach [C] me Thy [F] patience; [C] still with Thee
In [F] closer, [C] dearer [G7] compa-[C] ny,
In work that [F] keeps faith [C] sweet and strong,
In [F] trust that [C] triumphs [G7] over [C] wrong.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
In [C] hope that [F] sends a [C] shining ray
Far [F] down the [C] future's [G7] broad'ning [C] way,
In peace that [F] only [C] Thou canst give,
With [F] Thee, O [C] Master, [G7] let me [C] live.
{end_of_verse}
